    "result_text": "Done. I agreed with the finding and narrowed `MemberId.checkDigit(String)` from `public` to `private`, since removing the `checkDigit` response field/mapping left `format()` as its only caller \u2014 the Luhn digit is now purely an internal detail of how a member id is assembled. I trimmed its javadoc to note that. The public contract of `MemberId` is now exactly what callers use: `format`, `withSuffix`, `hash8`, `region`, and `UNKNOWN_REGION`.\n\nThe `{@link #checkDigit(String)}` reference in `format`'s javadoc remains valid (javadoc permits linking to private members). Tests re-run clean: `BUILD SUCCESS`, 1/1 passing.",
