    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe rename/merge is otherwise clean and faithful: old classes deleted, all references updated, the single-source-of-truth pattern preserved, naming (`AssignMemberId`, `MemberId`, `OwnerPrimaryIdentifier`) idiomatic, docs/javadoc/OpenAPI all updated consistently. One structural issue:\n\n**`MemberId.checkDigit(String)` should be narrowed from `public` to `private`.**\nIn the old `CustomerCode`, `checkDigit` was public *because* it had an external consumer \u2014 the `checkDigit` mapping in `OwnerMapper` (`CustomerCode.checkDigit(owner.getCustomerCode())`). This change removes that mapping (and the standalone `checkDigit` field), so in the production code the method now has exactly one caller: `MemberId.format()`, which embeds the digit as the `CHK` segment. The check digit is no longer a value the class exposes \u2014 it's an internal detail of how a member id is assembled.\n\nLeaving it `public` keeps dead API surface that advertises a responsibility the class no longer has. Narrowing it to `private` is the natural completion of \"remove the standalone `checkDigit` field\": the class's public contract becomes exactly what callers use (`format`, `withSuffix`, `hash8`, `region`, `UNKNOWN_REGION`), and the Luhn computation stays an implementation detail of `format`. (Its javadoc can be trimmed/retained as a private-method comment accordingly.)\n\nEverything else in the diff reads as something a maintainer of this codebase would write.",
